--- A function handed as a value is typed by what the parameter it is
--- handed to is applied with, however far it is handed on: through a
--- function that only passes it along to the one that applies it, and
--- through another one of those. (Compiled, a function handed on had
--- been read as text, and one never called directly was left out of
--- the program.) One nothing types is refused before the program runs.
fn double[x]
    return x * 2

fn apply[f, x]
    return f[x]

fn relay[f, x]
    return apply[f, x]

fn relay_twice[f, x]
    return relay[f, x]

log[relay[double, 21]]
log[relay_twice[double, 4]]
